# References only: NAME=op://vault/item/field. No value is ever written here, and no agent or CI job resolves one.
# Read by the stacks themselves (packages/infra/src/OpReferences.secrets.ts): on the owner's workstation a stack asks
# 1Password for the references its stage needs, through Alchemy's provider, and the app asks him to authorize the run.
# In a workflow the file is not read at all.
#
# The owner fills in the vault path of the model key's line and removes its "# ". The previews' line is written by
# `bun run beep infra setup --staging`, run by the owner, from an item it has 1Password make. Nobody else edits a line
# below.
#
# Production's model key (decision I5). Without it a production deploy stops and says so; DEPLOY_WITHOUT_MODEL_KEY=true
# deploys without a model on purpose, and production's rules then answer.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
#
# The one password every preview's test accounts take (decision "infra, a preview's password"). The repository's
# stack writes it to GitHub's `preview` environment as a secret; without it that stack and every preview deploy stop.
# PREVIEW_TEST_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
#
# The shared turbo cache (goals/ci-speed, step 9): beep-effect's cache Worker, team `inventory`. The tokens are made by
# beep-effect's token command (`bun token.ts --stage prod --team inventory --principal ci-pr`, then `ci-main`) into
# 1Password, never into a file. The repository's stack writes the read token as a repository secret and the write
# token to the `turbo-cache-write` environment, which only main may use; the Worker's address, which is not secret,
# is TURBO_CACHE_API in the root's `.env`. All three or none: with none, CI keeps turbo's local cache.
# TURBO_CACHE_READ_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# TURBO_CACHE_WRITE_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
